      "writtenOn": "2017-02-15T06:25:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My concern with this is that we\u0027d end up with a lot of if\u0027s in this part of the code. I\u0027d still prefer to have a \"command\" address (EXT_CMD_2 in my design doc), and then multiplex possible commands over that address (using the payload).\n\nThat would also make it easier to reply with some NON_SUPPORTED error code, or have commands that take parameters, etc.\n\ni.e. keep EXT_CMD-like format:\n\n    4 bytes      4 bytes         4 bytes       2 bytes      variable size\n  +-----------+--------------+---------------+-----------+------~~~-------+\n  + total size| block digest |    EXT_CMD_2  |  Command  |      data      |\n  +-----------+--------------+---------------+-----------+------~~~-------+\n\nWhere command is RESET, INVALIDATE_INACTIVE_RW, etc...",
      "revId": "bb5e81680482720d80f6dd7bed17ed5261b29aaf",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
